  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>evaluate_rag - runs the 15 questions of ../eval_set.csv through lab 21's retrieval and answer chain at two
settings, grades every answer with a judge model, and writes the per-question results and a scorecard.
Needs build_knowledge_base (lab 20) run first, Ollama with ${MODEL_NAME}, ${JUDGE_MODEL} and
nomic-embed-text, the pcm-pgvector container and a GENAI-EE license.

1. csvi-eval: CSV file input, ../eval_set.csv: question_id, question, expected_source (none for the 3 the
   documents cannot answer), expected_facts (separated by " | ").
2. emb-question: Text to Vector, Stream, Input Text Field question, Ollama nomic-embed-text at
   ${OLLAMA_URL}.
3. vs-kb: Vector Search, PGVector table kb_chunks, Max results ${TOP_K}, Min score ${MIN_SCORE},
   dimension 768, One row per input (JSON array).
4. dg-settings: Data grid, the settings to compare: top_k_1 (top_k 1) and top_k_4 (top_k 4).
5. join-settings: Join Rows (cartesian product), main step vs-kb: every question once per setting, 30 rows.
6. js-prompt: Modified JavaScript value, lab 21's prompt from the first top_k matches, plus context,
   hit_rank (rank of the first passage from expected_source, 0 if none) and facts_in_context / facts_total.
7. const-instruction: Add constants, run_instruction: lab 21's answer instruction, word for word.
8. ai-answer: AI Chat, Stream, message prompt, instruction run_instruction, Ollama ${MODEL_NAME},
   temperature 0, numCtx 4096, timeout 180, result llm_json.
9. json-answer: JSON input from llm_json: answer, cited_sources ($.sources), found.
10. js-judge-prompt: Modified JavaScript value, judge_prompt: the question, the expected facts (or none),
    the passages the model was given, the answer and found.
11. const-judge: Add constants, judge_instruction: list missing_facts and unsupported_claims, then the
    verdict (correct, partially_correct, incorrect, correctly_declined), faithful and a short reason, in JSON.
12. ai-judge: AI Chat, Stream, message judge_prompt, instruction judge_instruction, Ollama
    ${JUDGE_MODEL}, temperature 0, numCtx 4096, timeout 180, result judge_json.
13. json-verdict: JSON input from judge_json: verdict, faithful, reason, missing_facts, unsupported_claims.
14. frmla-scores: Formula, one 0/1 field per measure: answerable, hit, reciprocal_rank, is_correct, is_partial,
    is_declined_ok, is_faithful, is_wrong_decline, is_ungraded.
15. sv-results, txt-results: Select values and Text file output, eval_results.csv beside this file, one row per
    question and setting.
16. srt-setting: Sort rows on setting.
17. grp-scorecard: Group by setting, top_k: COUNT_ALL questions and the SUM of each measure.
18. frmla-scorecard: Formula, hit_rate, mrr, context_recall, accuracy (partially correct counts 0.5),
    faithfulness, decline_rate, run_date TODAY().
19. gv-models: Get variables, answer_model ${MODEL_NAME}, judge_model ${JUDGE_MODEL}.
20. sv-scorecard, txt-scorecard: Select values and Text file output, scorecard_&lt;date&gt;_&lt;time&gt;.csv beside
    this file: 2 rows per run, a new file every run.

Each run makes 30 answer calls and 30 judge calls. Change MODEL_NAME, JUDGE_MODEL, TOP_K or
MIN_SCORE in Run Options; keep TOP_K at least the largest top_k in dg-settings.</note>
      <xloc>160</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>629</width>
